Q: Javascript algorithm that calculates week number in Fiscal Year A: <p>Posting way later than likely useful to you, but this would have been handy to me!</p>
<p>I made one for the UK, should be adaptable to other countries if you plug in the start of your financial year. Maybe there's a simpler way of doing it, but I had fun!</p>
<pre><code>//attribution not requried, but appreciated. - Lachlainn Anna Hayes

function getFinancialYearStart(date){ //this is to get the first day of the tax year. 
    var month= date.getMonth();
    var day = date.getDate();
    var year = date.getUTCFullYear();
    if(((day &lt; 6) &amp;&amp; (month == 3))||(month &lt; 3)){ //this melted my brain. Checks it's either before April, or if it's in April it's before the 6th.
        return(new Date(year - 1, 3, 6)); // returns last year's april 6th
    }
    return(new Date(year, 3, 6)); // returns this year's april 6th
}

function getUKFWeek(date){ 
    var dateFrom = getFinancialYearStart(date); //grabs the first of april for the financial year of that date
    var dateTo = date; //wow this could just be removed, huh
    var dateDiff = dateTo - dateFrom; //gets date difference between those two dates. this will return as milliseconds
    var daysSince = Math.floor(dateDiff / 86400000); //gets the number of days by dividing it by milliseconds in a day. math.floor rounds down.
    var weeksSince = (daysSince / 7); //divides by number of days in a week
    return Math.floor(weeksSince + 1)
}

console.log(getUKFWeek(new Date()))
</code></pre>

Q: eclipselink PersistenceUnitLoadingEception in executable JAR A: <p>With EclipseLink v4.0.8: it is working fine if <code>META-INF/persistence.xml</code> is in its own jar.<br />
The problem seems to be related to the root of the runnable jar: the classes and the META-INF folder.</p>
<p>I can't explain it but I noticed it working too if <code>persistence.xml</code> is located in the root of the runnable jar and by forcing the path to <code>persistence.xml</code> like below. But it works only in the root of the runnable jar (not in a package or in the META-INF of the runnable jar:</p>
<pre><code>Properties l_properties = new Properties();
l_properties.put( &quot;eclipselink.persistencexml&quot;, &quot;persistence.xml&quot; );
EntityManagerFactory l_entityManagerFactory = Persistence.createEntityManagerFactory( &quot;WebScrapingFilmCalendar&quot;, l_properties );
</code></pre>
